  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong, cohesive dark editorial system with clear headline dominance, disciplined cyan/red/amber accents, crisp borders, and thoughtful responsive card reflow. However, desktop composition is excessively top-heavy and leaves a large inert right field; tablet/mobile body and source text are undersized and low-contrast; the tablet risk panel feels cramped around the CTA; and the global header becomes visually crowded, with truncated navigation labels and unclear horizontal continuation on mobile. These visible polish issues keep it below demo-ready 8.",
    "fix": "Reduce desktop dead space by tightening the hero grid, raise small-text size/contrast, give the tablet risk copy and CTA more separation, and replace the clipped mobile header rail with a clearly bounded scroll treatment or compact menu that preserves complete labels and an obvious active state.",
